LICENSES/wintun-MIT.txt
LICENSES/wireguard-windows-MIT.txt

VoCat can execute imported Clash VLESS/Reality upstreams through the following
unmodified third-party proxy core:

  Xray-core v26.3.27
  Project: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core
  Release: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/releases/tag/v26.3.27
  License: Mozilla Public License 2.0

The full MPL-2.0 text is included in:
LICENSES/xray-core-MPL-2.0.txt

The checked-in Windows ready-to-run bundles redistribute the unmodified,
Authenticode-signed Wintun 0.14.1 prebuilt DLL alongside VoCat, which uses only
the documented Wintun API. The accompanying prebuilt-binary license is retained
as dist/windows-*/WINTUN-LICENSE.txt. Operators using other builds obtain the
official, architecture-matched DLL separately under those license terms.

Those ready-to-run bundles also redistribute the official Xray-core v26.3.27
Windows executable and retain another copy of its MPL-2.0 text as
dist/windows-*/XRAY-LICENSE.txt. VoCat starts Xray only on demand for an enabled
VLESS upstream, binds its SOCKS5 bridge to loopback, and pins the executable's
architecture and SHA-256 before execution.

Material modifications made by the Windows fork are described in:
MODIFICATIONS.md
